A||N||21||Haze_Performance||Some Fiero owners SUCK!!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-06-2001||12:20 AM||||Well I tried... I was driving down the street (Dropping off the wife, to go visit her grandma) & a White Formula with stock white painted wheels passed me by going the other way. I was only a block away from grandma house.. My wife jumped out of the car & I started back in the direction of the Formula. 8 blocks later and I still didn't see him around. I came to my turn & stopped at the redlight. I look over to the left & there he was, parked in a two bit used car lot. I turned around to recruit a poetical PFF member. NO LUCK!! The guy (a older man) was walking back to the car & said "Hey Nice Car" to me. I said yours to. He said "It has the big V6 in it. Yours only has the 4 right? (in a sarcastic tone)". Yes I have a 4 in this one. He said "Its a rare Formula model. Its the only one that came with the smooth moulding.. It only has 79,000 miles on it, the guy I bought it from had it stored for a year" OHHHHHH This guy was being a PRI*K!!! I asked him if he was part of any clubs.. He said sarcastically "No way".....<P>P.S. The car was all beat up & when he started it, it sounded horrible!! <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-06-2001||12:25 AM||||you'll have that. Too bad more and more people are getting that way too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||04-06-2001||12:27 AM||||Haze, that "rare smooth molding" thing gets you every time!! -- I'll bet there is another one just like it somewhere though!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||04-06-2001||01:11 AM||||Most the Fiero owners around here are rather nice, I know 3-4 of em, the ones I've talked to were super nice. Most of em were like, My father bought one new or I've loved em since I first saw em. Man I love being a part of the Fiero community. But as with any community, there will be a  bit of a 'dumba$$' factor involved. :/ sad but true.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||04-06-2001||01:35 AM||||Haze, you shoulda made a bet with him about his rare car.. and then took him to your house to show him some smooth molding! hehe<P>Bet for pinks!<P>Glad I met the nice preacher with the SE instead of the jerk you met! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||HAGS||04-06-2001||03:44 AM||||I saw a 2m4 pass by going the other way on the highway and I spun around with my mom's Escape and chased after him doing 95 or so...took me awhile to catch him but I was able to get him to pull over and I told him about the Forum and the San Antonio Fiero club...gave him my number for more information on it since I didnt have it handy...told him I had an 86' 2m4 just like his that I could rip parts off for him and he never called.<P>It was a white 86' 2m4 Coupe, needed a paint job...he said he owned it for 10 years.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fyerstarter||04-06-2001||05:39 AM||||Lol Hags. You actually chase people down on the street and try and recruit them!?  Now thats dedication. <P><BR>Hayes you think some Fiero owners suck. ****  just be glad your not a part of the rice rocket community. I was into import cars for about the last 5 years and back when it started was cool, just a bunch of guys who liked to supe up their cars, now it's just a buncha punkass mommas boys who think their hard and that stickers make horsepower. It used to be you passed someone with a lowered car and they would give you a "whats up", now you pass a lowered car and they give a dirty look or scoff at your wheels because you only have 17's and not 18's like them or some ****  :\<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||04-06-2001||07:40 AM||||I can totally relate , there's a guy down the block with a black 88 GT , 30,000kms , 5spd. (my car is an 86) I have seen this guy at the local 711 on a few occassions...he always tells me I haven't lived until I have driven an 88 , and no amount of mods to my car could make it the machine he has(haha) he also has dilousions of granger that his car has 170 stock HP , but some people aren't worth arguing with.<P>In anycase one night last May at about midnight who should pull up next to me but mr fantastic himself (he is a mid 40's pompus ass) in any case were on a long 2 lane section of road , he puts down the window and asks if I'm ready to learn a lesson. I kinda laugh , roll my eyes. we both line up , I watch the opposing light turn yellow , bring the rpm's up to 2500rpm as it changes to green I drop the clutch , the 255/40/17 Kumoho victoracers (R compound autocross tires it was saturday night , autocross on sunday) Bite hard and I jump infront of him by about a car length, By the end of the intersection I'm a good car length up on him and pulling away .. I lift off and he comes up along side , I keep taunting him , he keeps looking over<P>Next light he tells me has been having distributor problems and he thinks he got a load of bad gas , because his car has the bigger motor (riiiiiiight)and his car is quite a bit faster..<P>He turned off at the next light , and took the long way home<P>Nothing like those ultra rare 170hp stock 88 GT's. <P>Some peoples kids<P>I won't even mention the kid with the Bright purple GT , with a cowl induction hood that is HUGE , neon lights under it , Lime green stripes , Just nasty..<P>To each His own<P>JM<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||04-06-2001||08:29 AM||||Not everybody is like that. For example, the one guy that owns the most Fieros in Barrington, IL, is the nicest, best looking, sweetest person you could ask for.<P>So, keep waving at every Fiero that drives by.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||04-06-2001||09:52 AM||||Easy for you to say Archie.. I don't see too many other Fieros in my part of the planet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Can relate to the ricer thing though..called rice burners here. And those stickers have got to be worth at least a horsepower or 2 for what they pay for em right?||||reg||6
Z||000010||StuGood||04-06-2001||10:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>Well I tried...  The guy (an older man)... said "It has the big V6 in it. Yours only has the 4, right? (in a sarcastic tone)"... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's not just what's said, but <B>how</B> it's said, isn't it?.  With any luck, someday this doofus may actually grow up, and learn to be a bit more considerate of other people.<BR>Well, as you said, you tried  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.<BR>  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||mbramble||04-06-2001||10:57 AM||||I purchased an 85 GT two weeks ago.  It has no doors, seats, roof skin, front fascia or headlight assemblies/wiring harness.  My son and I towed it the two miles home on a Sat and put it under the carport.  On Mon, when I got home from work, there was a prison road crew working on the road near my house.  They looked to be getting ready to leave for the day.  Before I got of the car, the Corrections Officer in charge walked over and met me at the car.  He shook hands and introduced himself and asked what I was going to do with the car.  What he was really interested in is if I was in the area's Fiero club and if so, was any member interested in buying his 88 GT.  You know, the one with the Lotus suspension!!  He was a really nice guy so I couldn't bring myself to telling him about his "Lotus" suspension.  Just kinda funny the things that are picked up by folks.  I'm sure I'd be in the same boat if not a member of this Forum and/or the Fiero mailing list.  <P>He didn't make any mention of rare round mouldings though!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||COUNTIBLIS||04-06-2001||11:18 AM||||There are several Fiero's where I live, I wanna say a black 87 gt, a silver 88 gt, a 86 red coupe, and several 84 coupes.  I can never get a chance to talk to them though, so Im going to put a "free ad" up at Wally world giving my name and phone number telling anyone that has a Fiero and wants to talk to another Fiero owner give me a call.  Maybe we can start some gatherings.  <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||04-06-2001||11:51 AM||||My bro-in-law works at a pontiac dealer and some kid brought in an 85 GT with the 4-spd not working. He paid almost $2000 to fix the trans because it was a "rare" car. He told him that the 85 GT was the rarest Fiero and he wanted it fixed because he was going to sell it. My bro-in-law said the only undamaged part of the car was the roof panel!<BR>A month later he called the dealer again and asked my Bro-in-law if he knew of someone wanting to buy it. Thinking of me he asked how much, The kid wanted $15,000!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>There was an ad in the autotrader for 2 months, same car, same price. Wonder if he ever sold it?||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||04-06-2001||12:10 PM||||Orief, I'm sure he did!<BR>Don't 85 GTs have the equally uncommon "ridged" molding? <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||12
Z||000015||firstfiero||04-06-2001||12:18 PM||||   Some people just drivem and don't love them like we do. Two days ago a fiero drove me and he beeped and waived. Yesterday I drove by someone else and waived and the guy looked at me like I was crazy.... To some their just transportation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> sad but true<P>------------------<BR>NO MR. RICER STICKERS DON'T MAKE YOU FASTER!!<BR> Todd<BR>    86se||||reg||9
Z||000016||LZeitgeist||04-06-2001||03:32 PM||||I'm much happier being an 'enthusiast' instead of just an 'owner'...<P>I wish there were labels that people would put on their Fieros to let you know at a distance which one they were...||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fformula88||04-06-2001||06:16 PM||||I totally agree with the comments about the import crowd.  I own a Ford Probe as a daily driver, and its actually a Mazda so it gets an import following.  Anyway, there is this high school punk who lives a few blocks from me with an identical Probe, except his is mint green (yuk!) and mine candy apple red.  For some reason, he's always talkin trash to me and trying to get me to race him at lights and such.  His mods... a neuspeed sticker on each quarter window and some yellow interior treatments.  I'd race him if it weren't for those stickers... they probably add 15 HP a piece.  The most ironic part is that neuspeed doesn't sell anything for Probes!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>These types of owners think they are better than everyone else based on their car.  Maybe if they were owners of a Viper of Porsche they would have a basis for showing off in that way, but these people usually have trash.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000018||Four-Banger||04-06-2001||06:35 PM||||We have an Auto Zone about a mile from our house that's open 24 hours.  Very exciting for when you need that little car part at 2 am.  The best part about our Auto Zone is that there's a guy my dad used to always see there that drives a fiero.  I don't know the year or model, but they always used to talk and the guy said he loves his car.  I've yet to meet a fiero owner myself that isn't nice.||||reg||6
Z||000019||FieroJoe||04-06-2001||10:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>I'm much happier being an 'enthusiast' instead of just an 'owner'...<P>I wish there were labels that people would put on their Fieros to let you know at a distance which one they were...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I totally agree!  I think that I have been the happiest I have ever been in my life since I got my Fiero.  I dont think I have ever been so focused on anything else.  I love working on my car and enjoy putting money into it!<P>As for the identification, get a PFF sticker!  <A HREF="http://www.fieroperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroperformance.com</A>  I think!...<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||WKDFIRO||04-07-2001||06:44 AM||||I would sadly have to agree that some people who drive Fieros have absolutely no clue about what the Fiero is all about. In the past, we would get a new member every once in a while who thought they knew everything about their Fiero. Even though they had only owned if for a few months. Most of our members are starving for info but some just have to know it all. And they usually don't know diddly squat. Sometimes people who don't even OWN a Fiero start trying to tell ME about my car!!!! I usually wait for them to finish talking and then unleash all sorts of trivia that only a Fiero Freak would know.<BR>"Oh...the smooth molding...wow...that is rare...oh except that in addition to the 88 Formula it also came in the 86 GT, the 87 Coupe, 87 GT, 88 coupe and the 88 GT. Then I would comment about his non-stock white wheels and lament about them coming in black, gray and then gold in 88 and how interesting it is that in they originally came with 205/60/15s in the front and 215s in the back..." Then just smile...<P>I try not to drive my Fiero any more on Friday or Saturday nights. Here in So Calif. the imports punk boys get brutal trying to goad each other into a race. Loud music, fart cans the whole works...if they are behind me I usually disuade them of any racing when I down shift into the high rpms and fire spits out of the exhaust tips (LOVE my cam...) Sometimes I just enjoy the quietness of being in my black 99 Grand Prix GT when Im out. Let the little boys play their games and crash into each other. Sometimes Im just not in the mood.<P>When it comes to other Fieros on the road, I should be more nicer...but more and more the Fieros I see on the road are just cars to their owners. I gave up waving a long time ago when I would just get a blank stare from the other side of the windshield. Now that I know that there maybe a few still out there (and even around my town) that care about their Fiero as much as I do, I might just try the wave again!<P>Oreif: Wow...having the only year GT that was a notchback means I can sell it for $15,000??? If only I can find someone with enough brain damage and money that reads the Autotrader!||||reg||1
Z||000021||87GT||04-07-2001||01:33 PM||||I love fieros from all years they were made.  The only owners that sometimes get on my nerves are some 88 fiero owners.  I constantly hear, or see comments on how wonderful the 88 is and how crappy the 84-87 handling and braking is and so on and so forth.  I have my 87GT and believe me I would like a 88GT someday, but my car is not a piece of crap and it handles and stops pretty adequately for me.  There are only a few instances of where the 88 owners were very rude towards others fieros because of how godly their 88 cars were.  It almost makes me wish 88s were never produced, but I like 88s so Im glad there still around.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
